  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Zanka finds fun in everyday simple things. One fine day he got interested in a very trivial sequence. Given a natural number kkk, he considers the sequence Ai=k+i2A_i=k+i^2Ai​=k+i2 so that the terms are\n\nk+1,k+4,k+9,k+16,…k+1,k+4,k+9,k+16, \\ldots k+1,k+4,k+9,k+16,…\n\nNow to make things more interesting, he considers the gcd⁡\\gcdgcd of consecutive terms in the sequence, then takes the sum of the first 2k2k2k values. More formally, he wants to compute\n\n∑i=12kgcd⁡(Ai,Ai+1)\\sum_{i=1}^{2k} \\gcd(A_i,A_{i+1})∑i=12k​gcd(Ai​,Ai+1​)\n\nDenote this sum by SSS. Zanka wants you to print  the number SSS for each kkk.\n\n###Input\n\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT, the number of test cases. Descriptions of test cases follow.\nThe only line of each test case contains a single integer kkk.\n###Output\r\nFor each test case, output a single line containing the sum SSS for the given kkk.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤1061 \\leq T \\leq 10^61≤T≤106\n1≤k≤1061 \\leq k \\leq 10^61≤k≤106\n###Subtasks\r\n**Subtask #1 (20 points):** t≤103t \\leq 10^3t≤103,k≤103k \\leq 10^3k≤103",
    "constraints": [],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n1",
        "output": "6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe first 2k+12k+12k+1 terms of the sequence AAA are 2,5,102, 5, 102,5,10.\nSo the answer is gcd⁡(2,5)+gcd⁡(5,10)=1+5=6\\gcd(2,5) + \\gcd(5,10) = 1+5=6gcd(2,5)+gcd(5,10)=1+5=6"
      }
    ]
  },
